{
  "result": "If I could change just one thing, I'd make empathy the default.\n\nNot the big, heroic kind of empathy \u2014 just the everyday kind. The instinct to pause and think, \"That person has a full, complicated life just like mine\" before judging, arguing, or scrolling past.\n\nSo much of what hurts in the world \u2014 polarization, loneliness, conflict, even just online meanness \u2014 comes from feeling unseen and misunderstood. If everyone felt truly heard *and* was a little more curious about each other instead of immediately defensive, I think a lot of other problems would get easier to solve together.\n\nImagine disagreements where the goal was to understand, not to win. Where asking for help didn't feel shameful. Where no one felt invisible.\n\nI can't rewire the world like that, but I can try to be a tiny part of it \u2014 by listening well, assuming good faith, and helping people understand each other a little better.\n\nWhat about you? What would *you* change?",
